From: easy-for-gaokun <noreply@github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] input: himax-hx83121a: fix asymmetric IRQ masking, add idle sampling

Two things in one patch because the second became measurable only after the
first was fixed.

1. himax_lock() masks the touch interrupt (quiesce_irq: disable_irq_nosync +
   synchronize_irq) but himax_unlock() never re-enabled it, so *any* sysfs
   access left the touch interrupt masked until a full chip re-init.  Remember
   the enable state across the critical section and restore it, guarded by
   panel_enabled / !idle_active / !shutting_down.

2. Opt-in idle policy: after idle_enter_frames contact-free frames (default
   7200 = about 60 s at the IC's ~120 Hz frame rate) mask the interrupt and let
   exactly one frame through every idle_poll_ms (default 30 ms); the interrupt
   path runs the normal algorithm on that frame and either resumes interrupt
   mode on a reported contact or masks again.  Measured on HUAWEI MateBook E Go
   2022 (GK-W76): 120.0 Hz -> 22.9 Hz touch IRQ and 2.00% -> 0.50% of one CPU
   core while idle, with no AFE command and no chip re-initialisation.

Also adds the diagnostic-only sysfs nodes used to establish the above: frame
(read one frame without interrupts, return checksums), irq_gate, regs (raw AHB,
gated by allow_raw_ahb), idle_state, and AFE mailbox read-back logging.

The reset of the idle counter is deliberately driven by a *reported* contact
(algo->touch_active) and not by a raw stable-track count: with the latter the
60 s threshold was never reached (measured: 7200 frames did not elapse in
111 s), because single noisy frames kept restarting the timer.

Base: drivers/input/touchscreen/himax-spi-core.c as shipped in
kernel-7.2.5-aoripus-ml-gaokun3-eog-el1-venus-r1/r2 (community HX83121A driver
plus the AFE transport patch).

Signed-off-by: easy-for-gaokun <noreply@github.com>
